//Port touch-look labels.  globalstrings1.loc loads inside StringResource::loadGlobalStrings'
//1..9 loop, while _overwrite is still true, so each line here replaces the retail string for
//its token.  Retail ships only globalstrings.loc, so this name collides with nothing.
//
//`sensitivity', `m_filter' and `m_invert_pitch' are not mouse-only on this device: touch look
//feeds CL_MouseMove the same SE_MOUSE stream (IN_TouchMove -> Com_QueueEvent(SE_MOUSE)), and
//CL_MouseMove scales that stream by cl_sensitivity and filters it by m_filter.  The retail
//labels name the wrong device, so they are reworded rather than re-bound.  Tokens stay as
//retail spelled them; only the display text changes.
MouseSensitivity										"Look Sensitivity:"
SetMouseSensitivity										"Adjust look sensitivity"
InvertMouse												"Invert Look"
EnableInvertMouse										"Toggles the look direction on the y-axis"
SmoothMouse												"Look Smoothing"
EnableSmoothMouse										"Smoothes out look movement"
MonitorSync												"Vertical Sync"
EnableMonitorSync										"Enable vertical synchronization"
